{"uid":"658f5667aa4a44cf","name":"test_a_worker_payload_reporting_a_tier_cannot_change_it","fullName":"tests.test_tier_escalation#test_a_worker_payload_reporting_a_tier_cannot_change_it","historyId":"3863ba624e7e1947b89230c98e024e68","time":{"start":1791867316004,"stop":1791867316037,"duration":33},"description":"A hat's contract has no `tier`/`effectiveTier` property at all, and\n    `additionalProperties: False` refuses one that tries -- proving the\n    field is genuinely harness-only, not merely unread.\n\n    v0.13 task 006 (#92 site 4) strengthens this. The OLD claim, pinned\n    here before the cutover, was: `sup._abort_reason and \"contract\n    violation\" in sup._abort_reason` -- a single schema-violating payload\n    was fatal on the FIRST offence, with no re-ask and no ladder at all.\n\n    The NEW claim keeps the old one's real content -- the payload's\n    `tier`/`effectiveTier` still never reach the record, the claim's own\n    escalation stands untouched -- and adds what the old assertion could\n    not see: the schema error was carried back to the SAME worker\n    verbatim on every re-ask through `contract_enforcement.\n    enforce_contract` (the EXACT SAME ladder sites 1-3 already use), the\n    ladder ran the FULL `contract_retry_max + 1` attempts (never fewer,\n    never more), and the outcome is an agent-fault iteration that\n    continues per the table rather than aborting: no `_abort_reason`, no\n    \"contract violation\" log message. With this test's one-iteration\n    budget (`_make_sup`'s default) already spent by the single charged\n    attempt, the run ends via the ordinary budget-exhausted tail\n    (`outcome == (\"tail\",)`), not an abort.\n    ","descriptionHtml":"<p>A hat's contract has no <code>tier</code>/<code>effectiveTier</code> property at all, and<br />\n<code>additionalProperties: False</code> refuses one that tries -- proving the<br />\nfield is genuinely harness-only, not merely unread.</p>\n<pre><code>v0.13 task 006 (#92 site 4) strengthens this. The OLD claim, pinned\nhere before the cutover, was: `sup._abort_reason and &quot;contract\nviolation&quot; in sup._abort_reason` -- a single schema-violating payload\nwas fatal on the FIRST offence, with no re-ask and no ladder at all.\n\nThe NEW claim keeps the old one's real content -- the payload's\n`tier`/`effectiveTier` still never reach the record, the claim's own\nescalation stands untouched -- and adds what the old assertion could\nnot see: the schema error was carried back to the SAME worker\nverbatim on every re-ask through `contract_enforcement.\nenforce_contract` (the EXACT SAME ladder sites 1-3 already use), the\nladder ran the FULL `contract_retry_max + 1` attempts (never fewer,\nnever more), and the outcome is an agent-fault iteration that\ncontinues per the table rather than aborting: no `_abort_reason`, no\n&quot;contract violation&quot; log message. With this test's one-iteration\nbudget (`_make_sup`'s default) already spent by the single charged\nattempt, the run ends via the ordinary budget-exhausted tail\n(`outcome == (&quot;tail&quot;,)`), not an abort.\n</code></pre>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"event_loop_policy","time":{"start":1791866910617,"stop":1791866910618,"duration":1},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"tmp_path_factory","time":{"start":1791866910618,"stop":1791866910618,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_isolate_ambient_home_in_process","time":{"start":1791867315981,"stop":1791867315989,"duration":8},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage"